    {
      "family": "contract:nf_inputs",
      "label": "Process input wiring",
      "named": false,
      "fields": {
        "$defs": {
          "Join": {
            "description": "How two channels filling one process input are matched.\n\nClosed for the same reason `Via` is: each member needs its own line in the emitter.\n\nThere is no default because broadcast and per-sample pairing have different cardinality.\n`.combine()` is a Cartesian product, while `.join()` pairs matching sample metadata.",
            "enum": [
              "broadcast",
              "by_sample"
            ],
            "title": "Join",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "NfInput": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "description": "One positional input of the process, and what fills it.\n\nA contract port is *semantic* \u2014 a typed thing the module consumes. A process\ninput is *plumbing* \u2014 one channel in the call signature. They do not\ncorrespond, and assuming they did is what made the first generated spine\nuncallable:\n\n- `subread/featurecounts` takes **one** channel carrying a tuple of bam *and*\n  annotation, so two ports collapse into one position;\n- `samtools/sort` takes **three**, of which a reference tuple and an\n  `index_format` value model nothing in the type system;\n- `star/align` takes **four** for two ports.\n\nDeclaring the signature here rather than parsing it out of `main.nf` is what\nlets the compiler emit a call for *any* module \u2014 a pegi3s image, an in-house\nprocess \u2014 not only for nf-core ones. Exactly one field is meaningful per entry.",
            "properties": {
              "ports": {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "title": "Ports",
                "type": "array"
              },
              "literal": {
                "default": null,
                "title": "Literal"
              },
              "param": {
                "default": "",
                "title": "Param",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "because": {
                "default": "",
                "title": "Because",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "empty": {
                "default": 0,
                "title": "Empty",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "join": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/$defs/Join"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null
              }
            },
            "title": "NfInput",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "items": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/NfInput"
        },
        "type": "array"
      }
    },
    {
      "family": "parameters:param",
      "label": "Setting",
      "named": true,
      "fields": {
        "$defs": {
          "ExtKey": {
            "description": "Which key inside the `ext` scope.\n\n`args` is read by all 10 vendored modules and `prefix` by 8. `args2` and `args3` are here on\n**nf-core convention with no evidence in this repository** \u2014 no vendored module reads them.\nKept because an unused enum value costs nothing while adding one later costs a `version:`\nbump for every archived `pipeline.yml`, and `MD0108` refuses a contract naming a key its\nmodule does not read, so a wrong inclusion fails loudly at build rather than silently at run.\n\n**`when` is deliberately absent.** It is a boolean that skips a process entirely, so a\nsetting could switch off a step while `steps:` and `inputs:` still describe it running \u2014\na second routing mechanism competing with resolution. Whether a step exists is decided by\nresolving the goal, not by a setting.",
            "enum": [
              "args",
              "args2",
              "args3",
              "prefix"
            ],
            "title": "ExtKey",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "MeasurementKind": {
            "enum": [
              "integer",
              "number",
              "boolean",
              "enum"
            ],
            "title": "MeasurementKind",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "ParamDomain": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "description": "The enum, boolean, integer, or numeric values a parameter accepts.",
            "properties": {
              "kind": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/MeasurementKind"
              },
              "values": {
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                },
                "title": "Values",
                "type": "array"
              },
              "minimum": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "number"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Minimum"
              },
              "maximum": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "number"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Maximum"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "kind"
            ],
            "title": "ParamDomain",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "Via": {
            "description": "The emission site. Closed because each one needs its own code in the emitter.",
            "enum": [
              "ext",
              "meta",
              "directive",
              "positional"
            ],
            "title": "Via",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "title": "Name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "tier_hint": {
